# Component Patterns

## Structure
- Export named components, not anonymous default exports, in shared files.
- Every presentational component must accept and spread `className?: string`.
- Use `cva` (class-variance-authority) for any component that has variants or sizes.
- Keep component files under 200 lines; extract sub-components when approaching limit.

## Styling
- Colors come exclusively from `src/lib/constants/colors.ts` — never raw hex strings.
- Tailwind utility classes only; reference CSS variables defined in `src/app/globals.css`.
- Use `cn()` from `src/lib/utils.ts` to merge conditional classes cleanly.

## Design
- Mobile-first: design for 375px width first, then scale up with `md:` / `lg:` prefixes.
- Bottom navigation is fixed at bottom on mobile (mirrors Flutter BottomNavigationBar).
- Follow the Flutter color palette: primary green `#10B100`, background `#F1F1F1`.
- Urbanist font is the brand typeface — loaded via `next/font/google` in root layout.

## Reusability
- Before creating a new component, search `src/components/` for an existing one to extend.
- `src/components/common/` components must be truly generic (no feature-specific logic).
- Pass callbacks via props; never couple a shared component to a specific API or store.
